In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Welders join metal parts by welding, brazing and soldering, and cut and remove defects from metal using a variety of equipment and techniques.
Tasks required by this job include:
selects appropriate welding equipment such as electric arc, gas torch, etc.;
connects wires to power supply, or hoses to oxygen, acetylene, argon, carbon dioxide, electric arc, or other source and adjusts controls to regulate gas pressure and rate of flow;
cuts metal pieces using gas torch or electric arc;
guides electrode or torch along line of weld, burns away damaged areas, and melts brazing alloy or solder into joints;
cleans and smoothes weld;
checks finished workpiece for defects and conformity with specification.

In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  We are currently looking to hire a Tax Semi-Senior in our Employment Tax team within our Tax Advisory Services division. We are looking for someone who has a particular interest in advising on employment taxes and advise both domestic and international businesses in relation to a variety of issues, including: 
• All aspects of employment taxes e.g. advising on tax-free employee incentives, ERR, BIKs, share-based remuneration, termination/redundancy payments, PAYE health checks and Revenue PAYE audits. 
• Employment tax compliance e.g. personal tax returns for inbound and outbound assignees, A1s / CoCs, share scheme returns, SARP related returns, etc. 

Key responsibilities include: 
Working with our team in Dublin, you will be given the opportunity to: 
• Work on a varied client portfolio, with excellent opportunities to develop and manage your own portfolio; 
• Be part of a dedicated team focused on employment taxes. 
• Become a technical expert in employment taxes. 
• Develop close client relationships; 
• Advance your people management skills; Ideal candidate: 
• You are AITI / CTA qualified or studying for these qualifications; 
• You have a strong academic background; 
• Strong technical skills and detailed working knowledge of employment tax and social security matters in Ireland. 
• A good communicator with demonstrated ability to work as part of a successful team. 
• You also have experience of reviewing personal tax returns for internationally mobile employees and associated applications (e.g. A1 and Certs of Coverage applications, etc.); 
• You are organised, a self-starter and an enthusiastic team player; 
• You can work efficiently to deadlines and encourage others to do the same; 
• You are driven, ambitious and passionate about continuous personal and professional development. 

Remuneration: Starting Salary for this position will be €36,605
Hours of work: 39 hours per week 
Location: Forvis Mazars, Block 3, Harcourt Centre, Harcourt Road, Dublin 2, D02A339

